==Alkaloids==
[[File:Laurifoline.svg|thumb|left|150px|[[Laurifoline]]]] [[Laurifoline]] [7224-61-5] is an [[aporphine]] alkaloid quat cation that is contained in ''[[Cocculus laurifolius]]''.<ref>{{cite journal | vauthors=((Tomita, M.)), ((Kusuda, F.)) | journal=Pharmaceutical Bulletin | title=Studies on the Alkaloids of Menispermaceous Plants. CII. : Alkaloids of Cocculus laurifolius DC. (Suppl. IV). : Structure of Laurifoline Chloride. | volume=1 | issue=1 | pages=5–10 | date= 1953 | doi=10.1248/cpb1953.1.5}}</ref><ref>Albonico, Kuck, Deulofeu., Chem. Ind., 1580 (1964).</ref><ref>{{cite journal | vauthors=((Albonico, S. M.)), ((Comin, J.)), ((Kuck, A. M.)), ((Sanchez, E.)), ((Scopes, P. M.)), ((Swan, R. J.)), ((Vernengo, M. J.)) | journal=Journal of the Chemical Society C: Organic | title=Optical rotatory dispersion. Part XXXVI. Quaternary compounds of 1-benzyltetrahydroisoquinolines and of aporphines | pages=1340 | date= 1966 | doi=10.1039/j39660001340}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal | vauthors=((Uprety, H.)), ((Bhakuni, D. S.)) | journal=Tetrahedron Letters | title=Laurifonine, laurifine and laurifinine, three new dibenz (d,f)azonine alkaloids from coccolus laurifolia dc | volume=16 | issue=14 | pages=1201–1204 | date= January 1975 | doi=10.1016/S0040-4039(00)72094-6}}</ref>
